[center][size=6][b][color=#ef6a5a]A G E N T   A R M O R Y[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4][i]Throw it. It does the aiming.[/i][/size]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HannaPanda/7D2D-Agent-Armory/refs/heads/main/nexus/images/SeekerHero.jpg[/img][/center]

Every explosive in this game asks you to be in the right place at the right time. Aim the throw, judge the fuse, hope they are still standing there in three seconds.

[b]Agent Armory[/b] adds gadgets that do that part themselves. Two are in so far: the [b]Cluster Seeker[/b], a throwable pod that follows you and releases autonomous drones when something hostile gets close, and six [b]throwable turrets[/b] that build themselves where they land. More modules are planned.

[center][color=#ef6a5a]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]This is a beta[/color][/b][/size]
The Cluster Seeker and the turrets are feature-complete, but the balance is still a first draft. If a gadget feels too strong, too weak, or unlocked at the wrong point, [b]say so in the Posts tab[/b].

[center][color=#ef6a5a]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]The Cluster Seeker[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Throw it, and that is the whole input[/b]: no pin, no timer, no arming. The charge goes off on impact and the pod is out.
[*][b]The pod waits with you.[/b] With nothing in range it follows you instead of sitting where it landed, so an early throw is not a wasted one.
[*][b]Ten seekers[/b] burst out when enemies come close. Each one picks its own target, chases it for up to 18 seconds, and detonates on contact for 180 damage in a 4 m radius.
[*][b]They split up[/b] and divide the available targets between them rather than all ten piling onto the nearest zombie.
[*][b]The drones are ground units.[/b] Stairs and rough terrain slow them down, and a target on a roof is a target they will not reach.
[*][b]Drone kills are your kills[/b], with normal XP and kill credit.
[*][b]Localized into 13 languages[/b]: EN, DE, ES, FR, IT, JA, KO, PL, PT-BR, RU, TR, ZH-Hans, ZH-Hant.
[/list]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HannaPanda/7D2D-Agent-Armory/refs/heads/main/nexus/images/SeekerSwarm.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][i]One throw, ten drones, and none of them waiting for you to aim.[/i][/center]

[center][size=4][b][color=#ef6a5a]See it work[/color][/b][/size]
[youtube]pQ4O9ZTpW90[/youtube][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]When to throw it[/color][/b][/size]
Against a tight crowd, a contact grenade thrown at the right moment still does more damage. What the Seeker buys you is [b]not having to be there[/b]. It works around a corner and keeps hunting while you back off and reload. Throw it into the room you are about to leave, not the one you are about to clear.

[b]It does almost nothing to blocks[/b], so leave the safes and the demolition work to the Timed Charge and the rockets.

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HannaPanda/7D2D-Agent-Armory/refs/heads/main/nexus/images/SeekerPod.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][i]Landed and waiting, with the horde still a street away. It keeps up with you until something comes close enough to be worth splitting for.[/i][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]Throwable Turrets[/color][/b][/size]
Throw the box, and an auto-turret builds itself where it lands and fires the ammunition it was built with.
[list]
[*][b]Gun Sentry[/b] (9mm HP or AP, Gunslinger): 120 rounds, 90 s.
[*][b]MG Sentry[/b] (7.62 HP or AP, Machine Gunner): 250 rounds, 75 s.
[*][b]Shotgun Sentry[/b] (12 gauge, Boomstick): 24 shells, 90 s.
[*][b]Sniper Sentry[/b] (7.62 AP, Dead Eye): 20 rounds, 120 s.
[*][b]Flame Sentry[/b] (fuel, Turrets): 300 rounds of fuel, 60 s.
[*][b]Shock Sentry[/b] (cells, Electrocutioner): 240 cells, 75 s.
[/list]
[list]
[*][b]Your perk ranks apply to your turret.[/b] A Machine Gunner build makes its own MG Sentry hit harder.
[*][b]It sees all the way round[/b] and starts out facing the nearest enemy.
[*][b]One-way trip.[/b] When the ammunition or the runtime runs out, the turret packs itself away, leaving nothing behind. It cannot be picked back up. A save and reload does not reset its runtime.
[*][b]It deploys on the ground.[/b] A box that grazes a wall or a zombie on the way down keeps falling.
[*][b]The Flame Sentry[/b] is a chokepoint weapon: 6 m of reach, solid damage, and it sets zombies on fire and slows them. Put it in front of the door a horde has to come through.
[*][b]The Shock Sentry[/b] is crowd control. It shocks and slows a zombie, moves on to the nearest one that is not shocked yet, and holds fire while everything in range already is.
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]Unlocking and Crafting[/color][/b][/size]
Every gadget has two ways in, and either works on a save you are already deep into.
[list]
[*][b]Cluster Seeker:[/b] the Explosives skill unlocks it at level 35, the same rank as the Timed Charge. Reading explosives magazines eventually unlocks it without requiring the schematic.
[*][b]Turrets:[/b] each one unlocks from the weapon perk that matches its ammunition, at rank 2 to 4 depending on the sentry. The AP boxes come two ranks after their HP twins.
[*][b]Schematics[/b] for every gadget drop from loot and turn up at traders, so a lucky find gets you there early. One turret schematic covers both ammunition variants.
[/list]
Everything is crafted at the [b]workbench[/b]. The Cluster Seeker takes 3 mechanical parts, 18 gunpowder, 3 forged steel, 2 electrical parts and 2 springs, and stacks to 20.

[center][color=#ef6a5a]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]Requirements and Installation[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Tested on V 3.4.0.[/b]
[*][b]EasyAntiCheat must be disabled.[/b] Single-player and private servers.
[*][b]No other mods required.[/b]
[*][b]Multiplayer:[/b] every player and the server must have the mod installed.
[/list]
Install the zip with Vortex or MO2, or extract the [i]AgentArmory[/i] folder into [i]7 Days To Die/Mods/[/i], then launch with EAC off.

[b]Before removing the mod[/b], wait until no pod, drone or turret is left in the world. Nothing else is touched: no blocks, no vanilla items, no world edits.

[center][color=#ef6a5a]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]Changelog[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][b]0.10.0 - Beta[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Built for 7 Days to Die V 3.4.[/b]
[*][b]New: throwable turrets.[/b] Six sentries across eight craftable boxes, each unlocked by the matching weapon perk or its schematic.
[*]Turrets cover a full circle, start out facing the nearest enemy, and keep their remaining runtime when you save and reload.
[*]The Flame Sentry deals solid damage and sets zombies on fire, with one flame that comes out of the muzzle and turns with it.
[*]The Shock Sentry works as crowd control: it shocks and slows one zombie after another instead of pouring fire into a single target.
[*][b]Fixed: a Cluster Seeker thrown off a ledge or against a wall could hang in mid-air where it touched.[/b] It now falls and deploys where it lands.
[/list]
[size=3][b]0.9.0 - Beta[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]First public release, with the Cluster Seeker.
[/list]
